    <body>
      <div type="work" n="346">
        <pb n="367"/>
        <head>346 — i — II. — <quote>Who shall go up to the mountain of the Lord?</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="preface">
          <ab n="1">Another on Priests.</ab>
        </div>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="2">Among<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> all those bound with flesh there is none who is worthy to draw near to thee, Lord; to serve and minister to whom is a great thing even for the bodiless hosts of the heavenly ones. But, since, my Lord, [having in <pb n="368"/> thy great mercy become man in truth without variation, thou wast in thy grace called<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/> our high-priest,<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/> and didst entrust the service of the priesthood and the celebration of the mysteries, the rational and bloodless sacrifice, and didst think fit and will that men [should perform<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/> this service to thee, with them<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/> deign to<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> set thy bondman also, thy priest, whom thou hast taken to thee, Lord, before thy judgment-seat (<foreign xml:lang="grc">βῆμα</foreign>) in joy; clad in the gift and grace of the priesthood<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a8" target="#n8" n="8"/>, according to the riches of thy great mercy.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 367, n. 2</orig></choice> Ps. xxiv, 3.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 367, n. 3</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>Of</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 368, n. 1</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>by reason of thy great mercy thou becamest man unvaryingly, thou wast named</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 368, n. 2</orig></choice> Heb. iv, 14, 15, v, 5, 6, 9, 10 <quote>And he became..... a high-priest according to the order of <persName>Melchizedek</persName></quote>, 17-iii, 3 <quote>Therefore..... ye have been called by a holy calling from heaven..... than his building</quote> (all with verbal diff.).</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 368, n. 3</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>to minister in</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 368, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>whom</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 368, n. 5</orig></choice> Unintelligible corr.</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 368, n. 6</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>service</quote> (?).</note>
      </noteGrp>
